    "question": {
      ":question/id": "4a0ecb55-01b9-57ce-b773-0cb83e82306f",
      ":question/problem": "Determine the number of pivot columns of the matrix $Q,$ given by\n\n$$\nQ=\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 1 & 3 & 2 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -2 & -1 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 3 & 3 & -4 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -6 & -3 & -7 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0 & 0\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$",
      ":question/worked-solution": "First, we need to convert $Q$ to row echelon form:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Q & =\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 1 & 3 & 2 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -2 & -1 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 3 & 3 & -4 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -6 & -3 & -7 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0 & 0\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & \\quad {R}_{3} :={R}_{3}+(-1){R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 1 & 3 & 2 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -2 & -1 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 1 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -6 & -3 & -7 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0 & 0\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & \\quad {R}_{4} :={R}_{4}+(-3){R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 1 & 3 & 2 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -2 & -1 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 1 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0 & -4 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0 & 0\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nLooking at the row echelon form, we see that $Q$ has $4$ pivots, and therefore the number of pivot columns is $4.$",
      ":question/difficulty": ":question.difficulty/moderate",
